# Text layout order for the shared libc.so link (lld --symbol-ordering-file).
#
# A read fault on a file-backed page also maps its cached neighbours in the
# same 64 KiB fault-around window, so resident libc text is set by how many
# windows a process touches, not by how many functions it runs. Unordered, a
# trivial dynamic program touched 32 text pages spread over 12 windows (about
# 800 KiB resident). These are the functions that startup, exit and the native
# C performance rows execute, most widely shared first; placed together they
# span two windows.
#
# One name per line: a C symbol or a hash-free demangled Rust path, as printed
# by the pinned llvm-nm --demangle. The builder resolves each to the linked
# object's symbol and records unresolved names in libc-shared provenance.
# This changes only layout. Derived by single-stepping each row's process and
# mapping every executed libc.so address to its function; refresh it the same
# way when startup or hot paths move.
<core::slice::iter::Iter<&[u8]> as core::iter::traits::iterator::Iterator>::find_map::<usize, crabc_core::vdso::vdso_symbol_offset::{closure#0}>
